From: ThorOS maintainers <noreply@thoros.local>
Subject: [PATCH] bridge: expose exact bounded MDB snapshots and fence writers

The switchdev MDB object contains only a multicast MAC and VID. It cannot
authorize native IPv4/IPv6 replication, especially source filtering and
colliding IP groups. Link the exact typed snapshot implementation and
fence actual multicast policy producers, not deferred lossy notifications.

Scope complete reports and timer/configuration mutations, including error
rollback and source/router/querier changes that emit no MDB notification.
Hardware offload feedback and read-only requests remain outside this gate.
Unknown control types and normal multicast data do not invalidate policy.
Periodic query TX only invalidates on real querier/address changes, rather
than exhausting immutable replication resources on unchanged timer polls.

Timer dequeue is earlier than callback execution. The snapshot API exposes
those time dependencies explicitly; its epoch does not promise hardware
expiry. The native consumer must trap unsupported timed policy to CPU.

